  "title": "Siege of Lachish",
  "summary": "In 701 BCE Sennacherib's Assyrian army attacked and took Lachish, a Judahite city, during a revolt led by King Hezekiah, who had withheld tribute. The city was destroyed and its inhabitants later deported; excavators found a mass burial of 1,500 individuals. Sennacherib did not conquer Jerusalem, and reliefs from his palace at Nineveh, now in the British Museum, depict the conquest.",
